[{'title': 'K12 Partnership Network USA - National Cybersecurity Alliance', 'content': 'RESOURCES\n\nINITIATIVES\n\nABOUT US\n\nABOUT US\n\nSubscribe\n\nShare\n\nLoading the Elevenlabs Text to Speech AudioNative Player...\n\nPartner Event\n\nEvent date:\n\n|\n\nAGO\n\nAGO\n\n# K12 Partnership Network USA\n\nK12PN (Partnership Network) is an inaugural event designed exclusively for K-12 leaders, including superintendents, CXOs, and key education decision-makers across the USA.\n\nSeptember 15, 2025\n\nEvent Concluded.\n\nK12PN\n\nK12PN (Partnership Network) is an inaugural event designed exclusively for K-12 leaders, including superintendents, CXOs, and key education decision-makers across the USA. [...] As the landscape of K-12 education continues to evolve, leaders must stay ahead by embracing innovation and fostering collaboration. This pivotal event unites top experts, thought leaders, and solution providers to explore the pressing challenges and opportunities shaping the future of K-12 education.\n\nThe 2025 theme, "Leading for impact: Empowering students and educators in a changing world," will spotlight critical discussions on leveraging technology, including AI to enhance educational outcomes while effectively addressing cybersecurity concerns.\n\nWith only 200 seats available, K12PN is an exclusive and highly curated gathering for senior K-12 leaders.\n\nRegister now to check your eligibility>> \n\nSave as PDF\n\nSave as PDF\n\n# Featured Articles [...] English\n\n#### Subscribe to our newsletter\n\n###### Resources\n\nOnline Safety and Privacy\n\nCareersand Education\n\nCybersecurity for Business\n\nCyber Dictionary\n\nToolkits\n\nAll Articles and Resources\n\nAll Events\n\nAll Press Stories and Awards\n\n###### Initiatives\n\nAI Fools\n\nData Privacy Week\n\nConvene\n\nCyberSecure My Business\n\nCybersecurity Awareness Month\n\nKubikle\n\nSee Yourself in Cyber\n\nThen & Now\n\n###### About Us\n\nDonate\n\nCollaborate\n\nRequest a Speaker\n\nSponsor\n\nThe NCA\n\nContact Us\n\n###### Special Campaigns\n\nCyber Survival Guide\n\nKubikle Series\n\nPhisher\n\nSafe Word\n\nThen & Now Site\n\nMailing Address: 717 Coliseum Drive NW, Winston-Salem, NC 27106\n\nCopyright ©\n\n2026', 'url': 'https://www.staysafeonline.org/events/k12-partnership-network-usa'}, {'title': 'The K-12 Education Conference Calendar: Every Event Worth Knowing About,October 2026 – September 2027', 'content': "Skip to Content\n\n · Nov 2026 (30) · Dec 2026 (12) · Jan 2027 (10) · Feb 2027 (15) · Mar 2027 (13) · Apr 2027 (10) · May 2027 (10) · Jun 2027 (10) · Jul 2027 (5) · Aug 2027 (5) · Sep 2027 (4) · International\n\n## How to use this list\n\nEvents are grouped by month and run from October 2026 through September 2027. Larger national conferences carry full detail: dates, location, format, registration, and the roles each one actually serves. Smaller and regional events are listed as one-liners under “Also happening.” Where a field reads TBA, the organizer has not published it yet—we do not estimate. [...] Back to top\n\n## About this calendar\n\n150 conferences · 140 United States, 10 international. Last updated: October 1, 2026. We rebuild this calendar on the first of every month: events that have finished come off, a new month is added at the far end, and registration deadlines are re-checked against what organizers have actually published.\n\nTwo rules keep it honest. We list an event only when the organizer has published specific dates and a reader can actually register for it. And where a field is unknown it reads TBA—we never estimate a date, a price, or an attendance figure.\n\nThis calendar also runs as an article on LinkedIn: The K-12 Education Conference Calendar. Follow Angles, Inc. there for the monthly update.\n\nMaintained by Angles, Inc.\n\n### Written By: Angles, Inc. [...] ### EDTECH WEEK 2026\n\nOctober 13–15, 2026 · New York, NY · In-person\n\nFounder-and-investor conference and festival at Columbia Teachers College and Bollinger Forum. Roughly 200 speakers and 300+ investors; oriented to edtech commercial and capital networking.\n\n LinkedIn: Company page\n Speakers: TBA\n Registration: early-bird closed August 31, 2026\n Who attends: Founders/CEOs; Chief Revenue Officers; Venture Partners; Heads of Corporate Development; VPs of Product; Chief Strategy Officers; Directors of Partnerships\n\n### ASBO International Annual Conference & Expo 2026\n\nOctober 14–16, 2026 · Pittsburgh, PA · In-person\n\nThe Association of School Business Officials International's annual conference for school district finance, operations, and business leadership.", 'url': 'https://www.angles-inc.com/engagecreatively/k-12-education-conference-calendar?hsLang=en'}, {'title': 'Events | The Partnership for Student Success', 'content': 'The Partnership for Student Success\n\nSelect Page\n\nUPCOMING EVENTS\n\n# Conferences & In-Person Events\n\n2026 Partnership for Student Success SummitOctober 6th, 2026 in Washington, DC\n\n Location: Johns Hopkins University Bloomberg Center, Washington, DC\n Register\n\n2027 Partnership for Student Success Higher Education SummitFebruary 23rd, 2027 in Washington, DC\n\n Location: Johns Hopkins University Bloomberg Center, Washington, DC\n A call for session proposals will open in late summer 2026 and registration will open in fall 2026.\n\n## Event Recordings\n\nMissed any of our past events? Pleasefind all previous webinar recordings in this section.\n\n## Are K-12 Students Getting the Evidence-Based Supports They Need? Findings from a Nationally Representative Survey of School Principals [...] Explore how corporate volunteerism is transforming K–12 education through innovative eMentoring and strategic partnerships, connecting professionals with students to inspire STEM learning and provide vital academic support.\n\nClick Here to Watch\n\n## National Partnership for Student Success 1st Anniversary Celebration\n\nHosted by National Partnership for Student Success \n\nClick Here to Watch\n\n## Collaborating to Accelerate Progress Towards Digital Equity: An NPSS Webinar\n\nHosted by NPSS Hub Digital Equity Working Group\n\nClick Here to Watch\n\n## Webinar: "250,000 Caring Adults, Rolling Out a New National Effort"\n\nHosted by Campaign for Grade-Level Reading featuring speakers from NPSS and others\n\nClick Here to Watch\n\n## Webinar: The NPSS Higher Education Coalition\n\nHosted by NPSS Hub [...] In this first installment of the Research-to-Practice webinar series, hosted by the Partnership for Student Success on July 24, 2025, we were excited to discuss recent research on live-online tutoring and how districts and nonprofit organizations can implement virtual tutoring aligned with evidence-based practices.\n\nClick Here to Watch\n\n## Webinar Resource: Tutoring & Student Success Coaching as Career-Connected Learning Opportunities\n\nThe Partnership for Student Success and the Pathways Alliance hosted a dynamic webinar exploring how tutoring and success coaching can simultaneously support K–12 student achievement and provide career-connected learning opportunities for those in these roles.\n\nClick Here to Watch', 'url': 'https://www.partnershipstudentsuccess.org/events'}, {'title': 'Events | K12 Future Collaborative', 'content': 'Learn more\n Virtual Roundtable\n\nFri, Jan 16\n\n  Discussion Topic: Curriculum Review and Implementation\n\n  Learn more\n Fall Summit 2025\n\n  Wed, Oct 01\n\n  Theme: Leadership DevelopmentDistrict Visit: White Bear Lake ISD 624\n\n  Learn more\n Summer Kickoff 2025\n\n  Fri, Jun 13\n\n  Reconnect, Reflect, Reimagine Live Virtual Keynote from Suneel Gupta!\n\n  Learn more\n Mason City Schools: Experiential Learning Program (XLP)\n\n  Wed, Apr 09\n\n  Details\n Spring Summit 2025\n\n  Wed, Feb 19\n\n  Topic of Focus: The Changing Needs of Today’s Learner & Educator\n\n  Learn more\n Virtual Roundtable\n\n  Wed, Nov 06\n\n  Discussion Topic: Elementary Literacy\n\n  Learn more\n Fall Summit 2024\n\n  Thu, Sep 12\n\n  Topics of Focus: Artificial Intelligence and CTE / Career Pathways / Work-Based Learning [...] Raytown Quality Schools, MO\n\n> The K12 Future Collaborative provides district leaders a chance to collaborate, network and be vulnerable about best practices andareas to grow capacity for your organization.\n\nAmy Cruse\n\nAssistant Superintendent\n\nParma City School District, OH\n\n> I appreciated the collaboration and relationships that I built with like-minded colleagues. I valued the professional learning and social time with district leaders.\n\n## Upcoming Events\n\nFall Summit 2026\n\n  Wed, Oct 21\n\n  Meeting the Moment: Courageous, Visionary Leadership District Visit: Parma City Schools\n\n  Learn more\n\n## Past Events\n\n Spring Summit 2026\n\n  Wed, Apr 29\n\n  From Admin to Instruction: AI in Action District Visit: CUSD 200, IL Student & Staff Presentation: Naperville 203, IL [...] Learn more\n Developing a Framework for Implementing AI in K12 Education\n\n  Thu, May 02\n\n  Details\n\nbottom of page', 'url': 'https://www.k12future.com/all-events'}, {'title': 'National Alliance of Concurrent Enrollment Partnerships', 'content': 'learn more\n\n## Professional Development that Expands Opportunity\n\nNACEP U is a professional learning hub for educators and leaders offering curated resources, publications, and expert-led webinars.\n\nExploreNACEP U\n\n## Upcoming Events\n\nView all events\n\n###### October 18, 2026\n\n#### 2026 NACEP National Conference\n\nJoin us for the 2026 NACEP National Conference, taking place October 18–20, 2026, at the Huntington Convention Center in downtown Cleveland, Ohio. Experience an all-access pass to innovation, networking, and best practices, with opportunities for everyone, from K–12 partners to higher education leaders, designed to support student success and strengthen programs nationwide.\n\nview details\n\n## Cornerstone Partners\n\n## Keystone Partners\n\n## Follow Us @NACEPtweets\n\n##### @', 'url': 'https://www.nacep.org'}, {'title': 'Holiday Calendar - K12 Private Academy', 'content': '### 2026-2027 Holiday Calendar\n\n| HOLIDAY | DATE |\n --- |\n| Labor Day | Monday, September7, 2026 |\n| Veteran’s Day | Wednesday, November 11, 2026 (student only holiday) |\n| Fall Break | Wednesday, November 25, 2026—Friday, November 27, 2026 |\n|Winter Break | Monday, December 21, 2026—Friday, January 1, 2027  (December 21st is a student only holiday) |\n| Martin Luther King, Jr. Day | Monday, January18, 2027 |\n| President’s Day | Monday, February 15, 2027 |\n| Spring Break | Friday, March 26, 2027—Friday, April 2, 2027 |\n| Memorial Day | Monday, May 31,2027—Tuesday, June 1, 2027 |\n| Independence Day | Monday, July 5, 2027 |\n| Summer Break | Tuesday, July 6, 2027—Friday, July 9, 2027 |\n\n#### Additional Support [...] ## United States Holidays\n\nAt K12 Private Academy, we observe various American holidays and in-service days. Whether you’re planning a vacation, trying to coordinate with school closures, or simply looking to plan ahead, we’ve provided the dates we’re closed to help.\n\n### International, Religious, andOther Holidays\n\nWe have a number of students who live outside of the U.S. in countries all around the world, and we understand that those students and theirfamilies celebrate different cultural holidays and may require additional days off. [...] Skip to Main Content\n\nflag EN \n\n flag EN\n Spanish flag ES\n\n• Need help? Join support sessions for enrolled families. Learn more.                • Earn AWS certifications with our digital pathways. Learn more!           •Learn more about K12 Private Academy. Sign up to watch our latest Info Session today!\n\nK12 Private Academy\n\nMORE INFO) SCHOOL LOGIN ENROLL NOW\n\n Chat)\n Call\n\n English\n Spanish\n\nSCHOOL LOGIN\n\n# Holiday Calendar\n\nK12 Private Academy students have access to our online system 24/7. They can find and submit assignments at any time. On nationally recognized holidays, however, K12 Private Academy is closed, and teachers and faculty are unavailable.\n\n## United States Holidays', 'url': 'https://k12privateacademy.com/support-resources/holiday-calendar'}, {'title': 'K-12 Education Events Calendar | K-12 Dive', 'content': 'The latest events, tradeshows, conferences and meet-ups in the K-12 education sector.', 'url': 'https://www.k12dive.com/events'}, {'title': 'K-12 Education Conferences 2026–2032 | K-12 Conferences', 'content': "💳 $350–$450\n\n📍 Eugene, OR\n\nMore info →\n\nK12 Future Collaborative Fall SummitK12 Future Collaborative Fall Summit\n\nOct 21–23, 2026\n\nFrom Tactical to Visionary: Leading Beyond the Day-to-Day.\n\nLeadership & AdminTeaching & Curriculum\n\n💳 Free–$550\n\n📍 Independence, OH\n\nMore info →\n\nSWWC IT² Conference 2026SWWC IT² Conference 2026\n\nOct 22–23, 2026\n\nSWWC Service Cooperative's IT² Education TechnologyConference unites instructional and information technology educators for two days of breakout sessions, an exhibit hall, and networking. Designed for Minnesota K-12 technology and curriculum leaders.\n\nEdTech & InnovationTeaching & CurriculumLeadership & Admin\n\n💳 TBD\n\n📍 Willmar, MN\n\nMore info →\n\nPASBO Facilities & Transportation ConferencePASBO Facilities & Transportation Conference\n\nOct 22–23, 2026 [...] Oct 16–17, 2026\n\nPresented by CodeVA in partnership with the Virginia Department of Education, the CS Innovators Conference brings Virginia educators together for two days of hands-on learning on AI literacy in education and integrating computer science into every classroom.\n\nEdTech & InnovationAI & Emerging TechSTEM & Computer Science\n\n💳 $100\n\n📍 Manassas, VA\n\nMore info →\n\nArizona Financial Literacy and Economic Education Conference 2026Arizona Financial Literacy and Economic Education Conference 2026\n\nOct 17,2026\n\nThe Arizona Council on Economic Education's one-day conference for K-12 teachers and administrators, running 8:00am–3:30pm.\n\nTeaching & CurriculumLeadership & Admin\n\n💳 $25–$100\n\n📍 Glendale, AZ\n\nMore info →\n\nEdTech Leaders Alliance ConferenceEdTech Leaders Alliance Conference [...] Oct 22–23, 2026\n\nAssociation of Teachers of Mathematics in New England conference. Explores innovative math teaching strategies, equity in math education, and curriculum development.\n\nTeaching & Curriculum\n\n💳 TBD\n\n📍 Warwick, RI\n\nMore info →\n\nUTSTA Conference 2026UTSTA Conference 2026\n\nOct 23, 2026\n\nThe 2026 Utah Science Teachers Association (UTSTA) Conference brings together K–12 science educators from across the state for professional development, workshops, presentations, and opportunities to explore new science teaching resources.\n\nSTEM EducationTeaching & Curriculum\n\n💳 See website\n\n📍 Layton, UT\n\nMore info →\n\nIdaho Early Math Learning Institute – Boise 2026Idaho Early Math Learning Institute – Boise 2026\n\nOct 23, 2026", 'url': 'https://www.k12conferences.com'}]

